# One Product, one workspace

Status: candidate mapping revision following the explicit user correction, 7 November 2026. Authority effect: none.

## Hosting rule

Each Product uses one operating home containing its Product records, Project coordination, Work, authority selections, ontology, architecture, implementation and documentation. Distinct Product, Project and Work identities do not require distinct workspaces.

Product development is coordinated in that Product's project area. Goals, plans, tasks, research, experiments, blockers and outcomes stay in its work area. No Product-specific development Project is automatically duplicated under workspaces/projects/.

A separate Project Workspace requires an independently justified operating scope. None is selected by the current map. The projects namespace remains available for a future selected initiative.

## Applied to every mapped Product

| Product scope | Coordination and Work placement |
| --- | --- |
| CyberAlchemy Lab | Root project/ and work/. Definition Formal Assurance is an embedded Project; the relational theorem-checker plan is related Lab Work. |
| Craft | workspaces/products/craft/project/ and work/. Preserve CA2-PROJECT-CRAFT inside Craft; remove the separate craft-development workspace proposal. |
| Define | Its own project/ and work/, with missing native identities explicitly unselected. Preserve the Lab-owned connector versus Define-owned source boundaries. |
| Ontology | Its own project/ and work/, including the existing lifecycle/integration Project. Keep both implementation packages and their distinct identities. |
| People and Teams | Its own development coordination and Work, if its proposed Product boundary is selected. Individual Person/Team records remain domain entities. |
| Lab website | Its own project/ and work/ under the current Product candidate; the independent Product boundary is still pending. |
| Trusted Dataset Materialization | Its own project/ and work/, without inventing an unselected Project identity or executing the Product. |
| Agent Reasoning Engine | Keep the referenced upstream Product implementation and coordination; no local copy is created to fill this template. |

TROQAR, Engineer Assessment and Agentic Research Network remain external. Their Product, research/modelling Project and Work share each existing external checkout. Lab snapshots remain historical references.

## Exact existing Project identities retained

- CA2-PROJECT-CRAFT: hosted in the proposed Craft Product home.
- CA2-PROJECT-CYBERALCHEMY-LAB-ONTOLOGY-LIFECYCLE: hosted in the proposed Ontology Product home.
- cal.project.definition-formal-assurance: hosted in the Lab Product home at repository root.

The formal-assurance plan explicitly reuses the relational theorem-checker analysis. That supports a navigation association under Lab Work; no new canonical theorem-checker Project identity or admitted Work membership is created. Craft formalization code keeps its existing source owner even when Lab Work references it.

## Shared operations and compatibility

Shared Lab operation implementations remain in root implementation/. Product-owned capability source remains in its Product implementation home and is consumed through explicit bindings. Runtime execution can be shared; specialized behavior does not require a dedicated installation.

This mapping changes no original identities, source records, Goal membership, admission overlays, frozen Define Packs or runtime selectors. The older Project-only profile still needs its separately specified successor. Physical source migration and native adoption are not performed by the catalog update.

The [complete folder structure](FOLDER-STRUCTURE.md) and [catalog](WORKSPACES.md) are generated from the machine source. The previous active mapping is retained as [historical JSON](inventory/workspace-catalog-before-product-colocation-20261107.snapshot.json).
